{%- comment -%}
  A setting's text in the visitor's language. While a setting still holds its English
  default and the store is shown in another language, the theme's own translation
  (locales/*.json, under "ms") is used instead, so an Italian or Russian page never opens
  with an English heading. A translation entered in Translate & Adapt changes the setting
  itself, and always wins.
  Usage: {% render 'ms-tr', value: section.settings.t1, default: 'English default', key: 'ms.home.h1' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign lang = request.locale.iso_code | slice: 0, 2
  if lang != 'en' and value == default
    echo key | t
  else
    echo value
  endif
-%}
